description:
File: oscore/src/edhoc/initiator.rs:280

Issue: The check `g_y_ct2.len() < KEY_LEN_32 + 1` allows exactly 33 bytes (32 for G_Y + 1 for CIPHERTEXT_2). However, CIPHERTEXT_2 must contain at least C_R (1 byte), ID_CRED_R (1+ bytes), and SIGNATURE_OR_MAC_2 (48-64 bytes). A 1-byte ciphertext will pass this check but fail later during signature parsing with an unclear `InvalidMessage` error.

Trigger: Malformed message with exactly 33 bytes (32-byte G_Y + 1-byte garbage).

Impact: Error is reported at signature parsing rather than at the appropriate boundary check, making debugging harder.

Suggested fix: Enforce a realistic minimum:
```rust
// C_R(1) + ID_CRED_R(min 1) + signature(48 or 64) = 50+ minimum
if g_y_ct2.len() < KEY_LEN_32 + 50 {
    return Err(EdhocError::InvalidMessage);
}
```
